add('rd-c21-t3-past-art',3,3,'Rethinking the Past · 艺术年代、研究争议与脑容量',[69,70],[72],art,['yes-no-not-given'],[
 q(35,"It seems likely that the Neanderthals' cave paintings were the first examples of artwork ever created.",'NO','Even earlier species, such as Homo erectus, may also have made art','Even earlier直接给出更早物种可能作画的证据，反驳尼安德特人必为最早的倾向判断。',YN),
 q(36,'It is very rare to find prehistoric artwork carved onto shells.','NOT GIVEN','may also have made art, for example by engraving patterns on shells','原文只举贝壳刻纹这一例子，全文没有very rare的频率判断。',YN),
 q(37,'The methods which the researchers used to examine the Rising Star cave system were rather unconventional.','NOT GIVEN','the way the results were released, in a non-traditional journal','non-traditional修饰发表结果的期刊，不是考察洞穴的方法；全文未评价实地研究方法是否反常。',YN),
 q(38,'It is unclear how old the etchings in the Rising Star cave system are.','YES','these have yet to be firmly dated ... more evidence is needed ... dating of the etchings','have yet to be firmly dated表示尚未可靠定年，正好支持unclear how old。',YN),
 q(39,'The means used to publicise the findings from the Rising Star cave system added to the controversy that surrounds them.','YES','The dispute has only been heightened by the way the results were released','publicise findings对应results released；added to controversy对应dispute heightened。',YN),
 q(40,'The size of H. naledi brains is a key factor in the question of whether these hominins were able to produce art.','NO',"I think the species' small brains are a distraction ... internal wiring ... equally important",'该题问作者观点，不是前人dogma。作者明确把小脑容量称为干扰焦点，不能把先引述的旧教条当作者结论。',YN)
],{'structure':['先列更早艺术线索，再提出H. naledi的争议；后段区分证据仍不足与脑容量不应主导判断。','两道NG分别扩大为频率、把发表方式偷换成研究方法；两者都不是看漏关键词。'],'phrases':['have yet to be firmly dated：定年仍未充分确认。','understate the situation：说得太轻，强调争议强烈。','a distraction：使注意力偏离关键问题的因素。'],'sentences':['However, it had quite a small brain ... and was therefore, according to palaeoanthropological dogma, incapable of complex behaviours. → according to注明这是旧教条的推论。','But other properties, such as the brain’s internal wiring, are surely equally important ... → But引出作者对只看尺寸的修正，问观点必须跟到这里。']},'保留原第4–5段；第5段跨PDF69–70页已按原句接合，不增删论证。NG已核对整篇文章。')

add('rd-c21-t3-past-preconceptions',3,3,'Rethinking the Past · 渐进变化与性别预设',[70],[71,72],ps(70,2,6),['multiple-choice','matching-sentence-endings'],[
 q(28,'In the sixth paragraph, the writer mentions mobile phones to make the point that','A','Evolution usually works by incremental steps and so does technology.','手机比喻说明技术和进化多为逐步发展；并非评价当代手机好坏。',MC,['A. most developments happen in a gradual way.','B. innovation can come from a variety of sources.','C. not all technological advancements are positive.','D. the path of evolution can often be unpredictable.']),
 q(29,"In the seventh paragraph, the phrase 'unpick this stuff' refers to the task of",'D',"Archaeology was invented by individuals with ... patriarchal views ... those notions fed into their research. Today's researchers are trying to unpick this stuff",'this stuff回指旧父权观念渗入研究，需要重新评估受这些观念影响的研究；不是指证据造假。',MC,['A. assessing the impact of certain recent research findings.','B. questioning the authenticity of evidence used in earlier research.','C. conducting research into how prehistoric societies were organised.','D. reevaluating research influenced by outdated beliefs about society.']),
 q(30,'What does the writer suggest in the final paragraph?','A',"Inequality, authoritarianism and patriarchy aren't inevitable. They're choices, and prehistory shows us that we can choose differently.",'考察史前社会揭示当代制度并非必然，支持我们选择更公平社会。作者不是仅说仍有未知。',MC,['A. Studying past societies could help us create a fairer society today.','B. We should not judge past societies by the standards of modern society.','C. We still have much to learn about how societies have evolved over history.','D. There is more than one way to interpret evidence about societies in prehistoric times.']),
 q(33,'An academic publication from June 2023 shows that','D','a meta-analysis published in June 2023 ... found women hunted in 80 per cent of them','新汇总反驳男性负责狩猎的旧假定；D谁找食物，B谁掌权不能互换。',END,endings),
 q(34,'Analysis of a 4000-year-old Iberian leader indicates that','B','an Iberian leader ... turned out to be female, not male as many had assumed','牙齿蛋白分析推翻领导者为男性的假设，对应谁有权力的旧看法不准确。',END,endings)
],{'structure':['以科技类比解释渐进变化，再把“预设妨碍证据”转到性别研究，最后联系今天的选择。','第33题是狩猎者，第34题是统治者；相似的gender主题不能代替对象核对。'],'phrases':['incremental steps：逐步累积，直接支撑第28题A。','get in the way of：妨碍；不是“为……提供途径”。','in line with this：引入与前项结果一致的新证据。'],'sentences':["The idea that there was a sudden explosion ... isn't inherently ridiculous ... But there was never that much evidence ... → 先承认可能性，再说证据不足，不能只抓第一半句。",'an Iberian leader ... turned out to be female, not male as many had assumed → as从句标出被推翻的是此前假设。']},'原第6–9段连续裁切；题面sixth/seventh/final paragraph分别对应本片段第1/2/4段。匹配题完整保留A–F。')

add('rd-c21-t4-hyacinth-problem',4,1,'Water hyacinth · 入侵植物与能源问题',[82],[84],ps(82,6,10),['true-false-not-given'],[
 q(1,'Water hyacinth was introduced as a decorative plant in east Africa.','TRUE','Belgian colonists in Rwanda, who liked the look of its glossy leaves and delicate purple flowers floating in their ponds','liked the look与自家池塘花叶说明最初作装饰用途。',TF),
 q(2,'Fishermen took some water hyacinth plants to Lake Victoria.','FALSE',"it had 'escaped' out of the country via the Kagera river and made its way downstream to Lake Victoria",'实际传播路径是河流顺流而下，不是渔民运送。',TF),
 q(3,'It is now difficult to force boats through the thick water hyacinth on Lake Victoria.','TRUE','the boats ... struggle to navigate through the mass of plants','struggle to navigate对应difficult to force boats through。',TF),
 q(4,'Chemicals produced by the water hyacinth plants are affecting the numbers of fish in Lake Victoria.','NOT GIVEN','blocking fishing routes and providing a new habitat for disease-carrying mosquitoes','文中说堵住捕鱼线路并供蚊子栖息，没有说植物产生化学物质影响鱼数；渔获难运不等于鱼类减少。',TF),
 q(5,"Cooking with charcoal has been proved to be even worse for people's health than cooking with wood.",'NOT GIVEN','About three out of four families in Kenya depend on wood or charcoal ... Using solid fuels like these ... increases indoor pollution','原文并列木材与木炭作为有害固体燃料，但全文没有健康危害高低比较。',TF),
 q(6,'People found it impossible to remove much water hyacinth from Lake Victoria.','FALSE','huge piles of water hyacinth that villagers had taken out of the water ... were a common sight','huge piles与taken out说明已移除大量植物，直接反驳impossible to remove much。',TF),
 q(7,'Scientists started investigating the possibility of using water hyacinth to generate biogas in the last century.','TRUE','since as early as the 1980s ... began to explore its potential as a biofuel','1980s属于20世纪；题面last century对应原文年代，不要求你查当今研究。',TF)
],{'structure':['植物起源与传播→妨碍捕鱼→烟熏和采柴压力→清除后作为燃料的潜力。','分清四组容易偷换的对象：自然河流/渔民，运鱼困难/鱼数量，燃料共有风险/风险谁更大，未能根除/不能移除任何大量植物。'],'phrases':['made its way downstream：沿水流向下游传播。','struggle to navigate：难以航行，而不是彻底没有船。','potential as a biofuel：作为生物燃料的可能性，区别已投入使用。'],'sentences':["But buried in those decaying waxy leaves was a renewable energy gold mine. → 倒装句突出被当废物的叶片中存在能源潜力；gold mine是比喻。",'Using solid fuels like these for cooking increases indoor pollution. → like these回指木材木炭的共同类别，不给两者排序。']},'开篇连续4段保留完整因果背景；两道NG另核对了全文，没有把片段未出现的内容当答案。健康数值只作为原考试文章陈述理解。')

